zation | 2026-08-30.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/explain-away-versus-fix-discrepancies]] | Adds the monitor-is-the-defect cross-link to the `0 nodes` rationalization and design-doc drift | 2026-09-01.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/compiler-backlog-hook-notice]] | Adds the 2026-09-02 coupling that promotes the backlog from latency notice to blocker: it causes the compiler repo's one failing test | 2026-09-01.md, 2026-09-02.md | 2026-09-07 |\n| [[concepts/five-slides-five-minutes-deck-series]] | Adds the PowerPoint-free renderer and layout-assumption cross-links to the three-direction rebuild and split-field default | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/automated-layout-qa-gate]] | Deck layout gate caught 8 bugs / passed 491 checks, but cannot see text overflowing its own box and false-positives on unmodeled split layouts | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/visible-regeneration-over-silenced-steps]] | Silenced/backgrounded regeneration served stale SVGs, a removed write let a page read first-run files, and a glob executed a sibling script — run regeneration visibly | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/powerpoint-free-pptx-renderer]] | Renderer reading `.pptx` directly after force-quit broke PowerPoint automation; preview spacing approximate, `.pptx` exact; Chrome contact sheet substituting for failed `cairosvg` | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/the-default-is-the-real-decision]] | A choice kept only as a flag expires with human memory; bake in the answer when the system can know it, bake in refusal when it cannot | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/preserve-the-prior-version-before-restyling]] | A restyle replaces an already-approved artifact; archive the prior build in a second location off the synced drive and ship new versions under new filenames | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/junk-node-contamination-minified-files]] | Adds the quota-cost argument to the 650-junk-node minified file, zero-yield-marked-done, and omitted `root=` findings | 2026-09-01.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/reviewer-unavailability-as-a-forcing-function]] | Adds the preregistration cross-link to the blocked-reviewer forcing function and the substitutable-vs-not distinction | 2026-09-01.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/alerting-path-must-not-share-the-monitored-systems-budget]] | Dropped lockout monitor events and the morning-briefing failure email both died because the alert path depended on the resource it reported on | 2026-08-06.md, 2026-06-18.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/s2-evaluation-preregistered-analysis-design]] | S2 offensive-line analysis fully designed before data existed: everyone-with-data cohort, max-absolute-deviation in population-SD units over Mahalanobis, absolute ≥1.5 SD flag, n≥10 room floor with renamed OL+DL fallback, 9 ADRs committed pre-CSV | 2026-08-08.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/preregistration-as-substitute-for-external-review]] | With no external reviewer, timestamped pre-commitment is the only safeguard; absolute thresholds pre-commit and relative ones don't, and the negative result must be pre-committed to publication | 2026-08-08.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/git-commit-identity-inferred-from-path]] | Git fell back to a home-directory-derived author name (\"Kristina Rash\") on the one commit whose provenance mattered — the pre-registration; fix is `git commit --amend` | 2026-08-08.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/applied-performance-biweekly-status-report]] | Report #1 for Chris Ruf/Kenny Boyd: honesty calls (unshipped vs registry, slip framed as deliberate, 4-of-17 blanks visible) and the dashboard-chrome→institutional-memo redesign in Charter | 2026-08-11.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/policy-document-humanization-diff-against-original]] | Diffing edited-vs-original revealed the AI slop came from the human edit pass, including a \"working\"→\"prevailing position\" hedge upgrade; three humanizer rules declined for register; deletion-type edits